# Styling

## Tokens

- Use established project design tokens (CSS variables or token files).
- Prefer reusable CSS variables over hardcoded colors, spacing, and type sizes.
- Do not introduce an unrelated design system when the project already has one.
- Brand values live in the project; Second Brain docs describe methodology only.

## HTML & layout

- Use semantic HTML.
- Follow responsive principles; prefer intrinsic CSS (flex/grid/min/max/clamp) when sufficient.
- Respect the section → container → column layout standard when building page sections.

## Accessibility & motion

- Maintain visible focus states.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Ensure contrast and interactive hit targets meet project accessibility goals.

Reference: `design-systems/` for token methodology.
